{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Plan review PASSED and is signed at d74d53a5ffd (0 blocking, 5 advisory). Two findings were dropped under veto:absence-refuted; both were checked against the tree and both are real, so recording the resolution here rather than amending the description, which would invalidate the fresh attestation.\n\nDropped finding 1 — not every relocated file is mapped to a target ticket. Correct: the plan names targets for three of the five. Resolved by measurement, so the implementation is unambiguous:\n- docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md -> epic hoary-datum-cop (0b32-bc94-5ea1-482a), named in the plan.\n- docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md -> epic hoary-datum-cop (0b32-bc94-5ea1-482a), named in the plan.\n- docs/88ab-feature-branch-evidence.md -> epic elfish-chair-lug / story will-tile-plum (2e8a-1a3b-66bf-4cd1), named in the plan.\n- docs/serena-symbol-reference-coaching-sample.md -> 84c7-ad6c-be99-4c30 and 9109-2ad9-2477-4cf6, the two ids the file itself carries. Post to 84c7 (the owning story); cross-reference 9109.\n- docs/dco-rollout-evidence.md -> story sepia-cardiac-hawk under breaded-ammonitic-elephant, the ids the file carries at :5.\n\nDropped finding 2 — no guard that all five comment posts succeed before any git rm, and no idempotency note. Also correct: step 1 is named 'Post before deleting' but states no ordering check. Implementation rule, binding on this story: post all five comments first, re-read each target ticket and confirm the comment is present and its body matches the file, and only then stage a single git rm of all five in one commit. If any post fails, delete nothing. Re-runs must check for an existing 'Relocated from docs/<file> @ origin/main 083620b08116' header on the target before posting, so a retry updates rather than duplicates.\n\nRe-measured origin/main after the review: it has moved to 7927904a0, but the only file